{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
  "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHARLES A. ROTHFELD, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I just didn't hear you."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The motion has been pending since that time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Republic of the Philippines",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Republic asserts ownership of these assets. Its, its submission is that President Marcos misappropriated them while he served as the president of the Republic. If that is true, then under Philippine law these assets at all times were the property of the Republic."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0000-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When a sovereign government cannot be made a party to a case because of its immunity from suit, that fact must be given great weight in determining whether the suit nonetheless may proceed. That is true whether the absent sovereign is the United States, one of the 50 States, an Indian tribe or, as here, a foreign state."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: We believe it would be dispositive in most cases, we think, only if the sovereign's interests would be adequately protected by the judgment or in the rare case that we've identified in our brief where the sovereign's interests are adequately protected by another sovereign, in the case of an Indian tribe being protected by the United States. But other than that, or where the United States is in a case against a state, the United States being the national sovereign, there could be special circumstances, but we think as a whole, the -- as a general rule, sovereign immunity controls."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Doesn't that depend on there being a foreign judgment, which we don't have in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Philippine Government",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Philippines Government sought these assets in -- beginning in 1986, obtained a freeze order in 1986, again in 1990. It got a final determination by the district attorney in Switzerland in 1995, confirmed by the federal court of Switzerland in 1997, that the assets could be returned. These assets, the shares, the Arelma shares, however, were not actually returned until 2000 by the Swiss Government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Swift",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I believe there is an important part of the equation that's left out of that question, and that is the rights of the Philippine government as the new shareholder will not be any greater than those of the prior shareholder."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Okay. You're saying -- I think you're saying that the demand would be ineffectual this time for the same reason it was ineffectual the last time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Swift",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Merrill Lynch can do what it did here, which is to file an interpleader and say: We want all the claimants to come forth and make the claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, but may I ask a sort of -- maybe it's too elementary a question, but has any court ever decided the merits of the question whether the Marcos estate or the Philippine Government owns these assets?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Swift",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0002-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The United Nations Human Rights Committee has even found a violation of international law by the Republic in preventing us from doing that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rothfeld",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is no doubt that the Republic has a substantial interest in the assets that are at stake here. And, therefore, its sovereign immunity, at least in the context of this case, should be dispositive and should have led to dismissal under Rule 19."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1204",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "2aae9e6ab554e3f09ea1ef2640ce5ce72a0173c7eb253756b44d1423f25197a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2aae9e6ab554-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Mr. Rothfeld. The case is submitted. [Whereupon, at 11:04 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.]"
    },
